      "comment" : "50000 - Remember soft-disconnected displays setting help."
    },
    "The app will forget all stored DDC values and treat all controls as untouched. Sliders will revert to default neutral values.\n\nThis operation does not reset the display itself." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Forget stored DDC values confirmation."
    },
    "The app will reset all DDC feature settings to their defaults.\n\nThis operation does not reset the display itself." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Reset app DDC configuration confirmation."
    },
    "The broadcast IP address for the WOL/WoWLAN magic packet. If left empty, the app broadcasts to 255.255.255.255, the local directed broadcast address (if it can be determined) and unicast to the device IP address." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Wake-on-LAN broadcast destination setting help."
    },
    "The built-in display is configured to be disconnected when an external display is connected. This setting will be re-enabled when the built-in display is manually disconnected again or the app is restarted." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Temporarily suspended built-in display disconnection notification."
    },
    "The built-in display of the iMac cannot be easily reconnected (lack of display cable, closable lid) in case of an application failure. Enable this setting with extra caution!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - iMac built-in display disconnection warning."
    },
    "The CUBE contains %lld color entries instead of the expected %lld." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - CUBE parser color entry count error; actual then expected count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The CUBE contains %1$lld color entries instead of the expected %2$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The CUBE dimension determines the LUT grid resolution. Higher dimensions provide finer precision but require more storage and processing." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - LUT grid dimension setting help."
    },
    "The CUBE dimension must be between 2 and 128." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - CUBE grid dimension validation error."
    },
    "The CUBE file contains invalid data on line %lld." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - CUBE parser error; placeholder is line number."
    },
    "The CUBE file does not contain LUT_3D_SIZE." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Missing CUBE header validation error; preserve header identifier."
    },
    "The CUBE input domain is invalid." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - CUBE input domain validation error."
    },
    "The custom filter no longer exists." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Deleted custom filter reference error."
    },
    "The DDC reset command might not work properly for all displays. You can also try using the built-in factory reset functionality of the display (usually accessible via the display OSD)." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Hardware DDC reset confirmation help."
    },
    "The default input source list reflects commonly occurring assignments, but the actual list varies by display vendor/model. Try using the \"LG alt\" toggle for some newer LG displays if input control does not work!" : {
      "comment" : "53449 - Help above the DDC input-source table for physical display inputs. The LG alt toggle selects alternative input codes used by some LG monitors."
    },
    "The device doesn’t support range-based volume control (i.e., setting a specific level on a scale between a minimum and maximum). It does support remote-style volume up/down and mute toggles, which works well for keyboard control. Volume control may not work optimally if an AV receiver is connected and HDMI‑CEC is handling volume between the TV and the receiver." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Remote-only device volume control limitation help."
    },
    "The device network adapter physical address used for waking it up from standby (using WOL or WoWLAN). If not specified, the app tries to determine it from the IP address of the device." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Device MAC address for network wake setting help."
    },
    "The display group is marked as exclusive while at least one other display group with higher priority is active." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Exclusive display group activation constraint."
    },
    "The display group will be activated or deactivated depending on the activation settings, configured group members and various other factors." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group activation state help."
    },
    "The display group will not activate when other displays are connected beyond group members." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Exclusive group membership activation setting help."
    },
    "The display is DDC capable" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - DDC detection result."
    },
    "The display may not be properly configured for DDC hardware brightness control and other similar features. Use detection and auto-configuration or adjust DDC settings manually." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - DDC configuration warning help."
    },
    "The display might have limited DDC support" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - DDC detection result."
    },
    "The display or connection does not support DDC" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - DDC detection result."
    },
    "The display will be automatically disconnected upon detection or physical connect if it was disconnected using the app beforehand. This setting might cause unexpected issues (connect-disconnect cycle with incompatible displays, lack of any connected displays) - use with caution!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Automatic display disconnection setting warning."
    },
    "The duplicated group will be disabled by default." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Duplicate display group action help."
    },
    "The imported LUT and its configuration will be removed." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Imported LUT deletion confirmation."
    },
    "The logical CEC address used for remote, volume and power commands. TV is the usual target." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - HDMI-CEC logical address setting help."
    },
    "The LUT file is too large." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - LUT file size validation error."
    },
    "The LUT is not a valid UTF-8 CUBE file." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - LUT format validation error."
    },
    "The LUT signal space or brightness range is invalid." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - LUT range validation error."
    },
    "The menu bar icon is aligned to the center relative to the app menu. Disable this for a more traditional look (align the menu bar icon to the leading side of the app menu)." : {
      "comment" : "53462 - Help for centering the menu bar icon relative to the app menu; this setting is unavailable in Sidebar presentation. Leading side means the starting edge in the menu’s reading direction (left in LTR, right in RTL)."
    },
    "The operation completed successfully, but some configuration changes could not be applied for the participating external displays.\n\nA new display group with the name '%@' was created and enabled." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group creation partial configuration success; placeholder is group name."
    },
    "The operation completed successfully." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Operation success message."
    },
    "The operation completed successfully.\n\nA new display group with the name '%@' was created and enabled." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group creation success; placeholder is group name."
    },
    "The operation completed successfully.\n\nA new display group with the name '%@' was created. The display group is currently not enabled.\n\nEnable and configure the created display group (including layout protection) under Settings > Groups!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group creation success and setup instructions."
    },
    "The operation completed successfully. Please apply the configuration changes and follow further instructions!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Configuration operation success with further steps."
    },
    "The operation could not be performed at this time." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Temporarily unavailable operation error."
    },
    "The operation could not be performed." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Operation failure message."
    },
    "The operation might cause the screen to flicker and switch modes if the existing mode is not available with the factory EDID. The display will be redetected as a different display if the current EDID has different identifiers.\n\nIn case of a failure, disconnect and reconnect the display physically." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Restore factory EDID confirmation warning."
    },
    "The operation might cause the screen to flicker and switch modes if the existing mode is not available with the updated EDID. The display will be redetected as a different display if the EDID has different identifiers.\n\nIn case of a failure, disconnect and reconnect the display physically." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Apply updated EDID confirmation warning."
    },
    "The original CUBE source is compressed and stored with BetterDisplay settings so it remains portable and can be exported later." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Imported LUT source storage help."
    },
    "The physical dimension (used to calculate UI scaling) associated with a virtual screen is determined primarily by the 'reported diagonal size' setting which can be further modified by the 'display physical dimensions' setting when the virtual screen is connected." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual display physical size configuration help."
    },
    "The physical dimension (used to calculate UI scaling) associated with a virtual screen is determined primarily by the 'reported diagonal size' setting which can be further modified by the `display physical dimensions` setting when the virtual screen is connected." : {
      "comment" : "53430 - Help for Watch virtual screens in group UI scale matching. Display physical dimensions is a visible setting label, not code; quote the label naturally rather than requiring monospace formatting."
    },
    "The privileged helper did not reply in time." : {
      "comment" : "52329 - Error shown when the privileged helper does not respond to the app within the allowed time. ‘Privileged helper’ is the app’s background system service for administrator-level operations."
    },
    "The privileged helper is missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "52329 - Error shown when the privileged helper executable or its launch daemon configuration is absent from the app bundle. ‘Privileged helper’ is the app’s background system service for administrator-level operations."
    },
    "The privileged helper needs to be refreshed." : {
      "comment" : "52329 - Error shown when the installed privileged helper version does not match the app and must be re-registered. ‘Refreshed’ means replacing or updating the helper registration, not refreshing the user interface."
    },
    "The slider will omit resolutions that do not match the display's size in order to reduce clutter and make the slider easier to use. Affects resolution keyboard shortcuts as well." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Resolution slider filtering setting help."
    },
    "The source selection does not contain any content." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Empty capture source selection error."
    },
    "The stored custom filter record is invalid." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Custom filter persistence validation error."
    },
    "The stored LUT data is missing or damaged." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Stored LUT data validation error."
    },
    "The system might reconnect the built-in display and other displays after wake from sleep to ensure GUI access. With this option enabled, the app forcefully disconnects these displays again. Post-wake main display will not be disconnected." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Force display disconnection after system wake setting help."
    },
    "The time it takes for the app to enter into an active state after the system wakes from a sleep." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Post-wake activation delay setting help."
    },
    "The time it takes for the app to respond to a configuration change." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Configuration response delay setting help."
    },
    "The TV requires pairing" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - TV pairing requirement state."
    },
    "The virtual screen created with this aspect ratio does not seem to be viable." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Unsupported virtual screen aspect ratio error."
    },
    "The virtual screen is now associated with a display and to comply with association settings, the virtual screen should automatically change its connection status. Alternatively you can disable auto-connect (it can be enabled any time under association settings)." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen association connection change prompt."
    },
    "The virtual screen was not created." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen creation error."
    },
    "There are fewer than two display group members present." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group activation constraint."
    },
    "There are no display group members present." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group activation constraint."
    },
    "There are some unapplied system configuration changes." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Pending system configuration changes warning."
    },
    "There is at least one controllable display connected" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display group activation condition."
    },
    "There is no group member present." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Missing display group member status."
    },
    "Thermal" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Core Image Thermal false-color image filter."
    },
    "These three identifiers (serial number, vendor and model ID) serve as the basis for display identification in macOS. If any of these three identifiers are changed, the system will assign a new identity (UUID) to the virtual screen and treat it as a newly connected display." : {
      "comment" : "53454 - Help below the virtual-screen serial number, vendor ID and model ID fields. Changing any identifier makes macOS assign a new UUID and recognize the virtual screen as a new display."
    },
    "Third pass WOL attempt delay" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Third Wake-on-LAN attempt delay setting."
    },
    "Third-party external display" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Non-Apple external display type."
    },
    "This allows additional image adjustment control options when color table adjustments are not enabled or available. Comes with a slight performance penalty. This feature is always active when software brightness upscaling is turned on while color table adjustments are not available." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Metal image adjustment fallback help."
    },
    "This allows advanced dimming, color adjustments and other features like software XDR/HDR upscaling. Note: color adjustments clip HDR content when in active use. If this option is disabled, the app will fall back to overlay based dimming control and uses Metal for software XDR/HDR upscaling." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Color table control setting help."
    },
    "This allows power control on physical connect/disconnect (or when the device is detected/undetected for other reasons)." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Device power control on detection setting help."
    },
    "This allows the dimming or image adjustment overlay to take effect on the lock screen and on spaces where it is normally ineffective." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Overlay coverage on lock screen and spaces help."
    },
    "This applies both to physically connecting an external display and using the app to reconnect one. However, the app will not reconnect the built-in display if you allow all displays to be disconnected!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Built-in display reconnection behavior help."
    },
    "This can be a result of disabled DDC/CI support (check the display's OSD), display firmware limitations or connection issues. Many TVs and TV-derived smart monitors do not support DDC. If the issue cannot be resolved either by changing display settings or fixing cable issues, you should disable DDC support." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - DDC unsupported detection troubleshooting help."
    },
    "This configures how the data associated with the currently configured display is matched to a detected display during the configuration/detection process. Changing this setting might cause a display to be recognized as previously unconnected and disassociate existing saved display configuration data. System UUID match uses the macOS default identification. When set to use basic identifiers, the app identifies the display by its vendor/model IDs and serial number. With extended it also uses product name, alphanumeric serial number, and production date. With port and location the app also considers hardware connectivity data." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Display identification method setting help."
    },
    "This control is now a placeholder and does not perform any action." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Unconfigured custom control status."
    },
    "This custom control is configured for one or more displays or display groups. Deleting it will also remove it from them." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Custom control deletion confirmation."
    },
    "This display group has no member displays." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Empty display group status."
    },
    "This display is the main display. Are you sure you want to turn the display off?\n\nPlease note that not all displays support DDC power operations and some displays may not behave as expected. If you power off your display, you will have to power it back on manually." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Main display hardware power-off confirmation."
    },
    "This display is the main display. Are you sure you want to turn the screen off?" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Main screen off confirmation."
    },
    "This format string specifies how the control's internal value is formatted and sent to the device." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Integration control output format help."
    },
    "This is in addition to the configured wake delay (%@ seconds), configuration delay (%@ seconds) and the time it takes to configure the displays." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Additional delay help; placeholders are wake and configuration delay seconds.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "This is in addition to the configured wake delay (%1$@ seconds), configuration delay (%2$@ seconds) and the time it takes to configure the displays."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This is required for color adjustments and a better software dimming and XDR/HDR upscaling experience. Recommended to leave enabled. Turn this off for compatibility with some third party apps that also alter system colors." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Color table control compatibility help."
    },
    "This is the default display group. This group cannot be removed but can be disabled or made inactive by changing activation settings." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Default display group constraint help."
    },
    "This is the recommended setting." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Recommended setting help."
    },
    "This keyboard shortcut is already used by the menu item \"%@\"." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Keyboard shortcut conflict; placeholder is menu item name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "This keyboard shortcut is already used by the menu item “%@”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This keyboard shortcut is used by the system." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - System keyboard shortcut conflict.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "This keyboard shortcut is used by the system."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This license was originally issued for an earlier version of %@ and has already been extended once with a complimentary upgrade to a subsequent major version.\n\nThis license no longer covers the current app version (v%@). To continue using this version of %@, please purchase a new license.\n\nTo ensure a smooth app upgrade experience, your current activation will remain valid until you deactivate. Please note: once deactivated or reinstalled, this app version cannot be reactivated with this license.\n\nThank you for your understanding and continued support." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - License upgrade eligibility notice; placeholders are app name, version, and app name in that order.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "This license was originally issued for an earlier version of %1$@ and has already been extended once with a complimentary upgrade to a subsequent major version.\n\nThis license no longer covers the current app version (v%2$@). To continue using this version of %3$@, please purchase a new license.\n\nTo ensure a smooth app upgrade experience, your current activation will remain valid until you deactivate. Please note: once deactivated or reinstalled, this app version cannot be reactivated with this license.\n\nThank you for your understanding and continued support."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This LUT is enabled for %lld display or stream configurations. Deleting it will disable those assignments as well." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - LUT in-use deletion warning; placeholder is assignment count."
    },
    "This menu item is redundant if the header is set to present the function as a switch." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Menu visibility redundancy help."
    },
    "This might help solve issues with certain configurations." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Compatibility workaround setting help."
    },
    "This might not work properly with every display, especially low-PPI displays, and may produce a pixel-doubled LoDPI default resolution instead." : {
      "comment" : "53438 - Warning for the Intel-only Aim for a HiDPI default resolution system display override setting. PPI means pixels per inch; on some displays the resulting default may be pixel-doubled LoDPI instead of HiDPI."
    },
    "This might serve as a workaround for the stream/PIP confusion issue exhibited by some configurations when multiple virtual screens are connected." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen streaming workaround help."
    },
    "This name identifies the LUT in the repository and filter menus. Each custom filter must have a unique name." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Custom LUT filter name field help."
    },
    "This name is used by macOS system-wide." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - System display name field help."
    },
    "This operation will disconnect and reconnect all currently connected virtual screens!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen reconnect all confirmation."
    },
    "This prevents momentary brightness fluctuations after HDR content was presented on the display. Please note that while keeping the built-in display in EDR mode for direct brightness control does not have any drawbacks, this setting may force other external Apple displays into EDR mode as well." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Keep display in EDR mode setting help."
    },
    "This provides a cleaner look when sliders are not in active use." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Hide inactive slider labels setting help."
    },
    "This resolution is used as the default (as HiDPI if available) when the display is included in a new layout." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Default layout resolution setting help."
    },
    "This resolution is used as the default when the display is included in a new layout. Results might be approximate on Intel Macs." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Default layout resolution setting help."
    },
    "This restores the default settings and restarts the app.\n\nPlease note that previously stored custom display configurations won't be removed from the system!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Reset app settings confirmation."
    },
    "This setting applies to screens/displays that are scalable (virtual screens, real displays with flexible scaling enabled). Default resolution is 100⁠%." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Scalable display percentage setting help."
    },
    "This should match the physical resolution of the display panel (actual number of pixels vertically and horizontally)." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Native pixel resolution setting help."
    },
    "This should remove displays from the display layout and make them enter standby mode on compatible systems.\n\nSome displays are not compatible with this feature and may not turn off or remain turned off.\n\nIf you can't turn the display back on using the app, try reconnecting the display manually (or in case of the MacBook display, close and open the lid)." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Multiple display soft disconnection confirmation and recovery help."
    },
    "This should remove the display from the display layout and make the display enter standby mode.\n\nSome displays are not compatible with this feature and may not turn off or remain off.\n\nIf you can't turn the display back on using the app, try reconnecting the display manually (or in case of the MacBook display, close and open the lid)." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Single display soft disconnection confirmation and recovery help."
    },
    "This should remove the display from the display layout.\n\nOn Intel Macs, soft-disconnecting a display does not put it fully to sleep and may not work as expected. While it is disconnected through the app, physically turning it off, unplugging it, or closing the built-in display lid can leave the Mac without a display until restart." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Intel Mac soft disconnection warning."
    },
    "This upscaling method expands the available brightness range for SDR content and allows HDR without clipping by directly controlling the display's brightness. Incompatible with the default brightness control features of macOS. Make sure the app properly listens to the keyboard brightness control keys." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Direct brightness upscaling method help."
    },
    "This virtual screen cannot be manually connected!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Associated virtual screen manual connection constraint."
    },
    "This virtual screen cannot be manually disconnected!" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Associated virtual screen manual disconnection constraint."
    },
    "This virtual screen needs to be reconnected for all configuration changes to take place! During this operation the display will not be available for a moment!\n\nYou can dismiss this notification - in this case the changes will be applied when the virtual screen is connected next time." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen pending configuration reconnect notification."
    },
    "This virtual screen should now be connected" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen association connection prompt."
    },
    "This virtual screen should now be disconnected" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Virtual screen association disconnection prompt."
    },
    "This will appear as the control's name throughout the app. Should be unique to avoid confusion." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Custom control name field help."
    },
    "Timeout" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Operation timeout setting."
    },
    "times" : {
      "comment" : "53449 - Repetition count unit shown after a numeric field, such as DDC command send and retry counts. Translate as a unit following the number, not as a count label."
    },
    "Title Bar & Window Controls" : {
      "comment" : "53449 - Toggle for showing the title bar and window controls in PIP, selected-content stream, and filter windows. Keep this menu label compact."
    },
    "To control features that have an on/off state. Can be used for group-level synchronization." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Boolean integration control help."
    },
    "To control features that operate on a range (like brightness). Can be used for group-level synchronization." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Range integration control help."
    },
    "To make your Apple keyboard's brightness and volume keys control your external display, please add the app to **System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility**! After this, you'll have to restart the app. Alternatively, you can disable native keyboard control in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Native keyboard control Accessibility permission instructions."
    },
    "To make your Apple keyboard's brightness and volume keys control your external display, please add the app to **System Settings > Privacy & Security > Device Control and Data Access**! After this, you'll have to restart the app. Alternatively, you can disable native keyboard control in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Native keyboard control macOS 27 permission instructions."
    },
    "To open Settings, use the Tools menu, hold ⌥ Option while clicking on the app menu icon or launch the app again while it is already running." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Open app settings instructions."
    },
