    "When Expanded" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Expanded menu state visibility option."
    },
    "When expanding a menu item, automatically hide other items under the given device / menu block. This helps keep the menu smaller." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Menu automatic collapse setting help."
    },
    "When HDR upscaling is enabled while hardware brightness control is disabled, the app uses a continuous brightness scale between zero and the calibrated max upscale value. Due to this the neutral setting (100⁠% brightness, when on-screen HDR content is unclipped) might not fall to an OSD chiclet boundary which makes it difficult to attain via the shortcut keys. To fix this an additional mid-chiclet step at 100⁠% brightness is inserted." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Neutral software HDR brightness keyboard step setting help."
    },
    "When Settings is Open" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Settings-dependent visibility option."
    },
    "When the app detects that the active audio device supports native volume control in macOS while it listens to media keys, it forwards the appropriate operations to the operating system." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Native media key audio handling help."
    },
    "When the display is set as main, the lower limit is 30⁠% for combined or software brightness, 10⁠% for Apple hardware brightness, 0⁠% for DDC hardware brightness." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Main display safe minimum brightness help."
    },
    "When this is enabled, syncing won't affect displays in HDR mode or XDR displays set to a reference Apple Display Preset." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Skip HDR/reference XDR synchronization setting help."
    },
    "When this is enabled, the app will use hardware brightness for combined brightness control instead of the SDR peak brightness adjustment control (HDR brightness control) provided by macOS. You can still adjust the SDR peak brightness in Control Center - these adjustments will influence the upscaling (if available) headroom provided by the app. Not all displays support hardware brightness control in HDR mode." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Prefer hardware brightness in HDR setting help."
    },
    "When this is enabled, the app will use the matching audio device's native audio controls (if available) instead of direct hardware control (via DDC or control integration). Make sure the matching audio device name is specified accordingly. This feature is useful for controlling the volume of multi-output audio devices involving both displays with app-managed hardware (DDC, control integration) volume control and displays with native volume control." : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Prefer associated native audio device volume control setting help."
    },
    "When volume reaches 0⁠%…" : {
      "comment" : "50000 - Zero volume behavior setting heading."
    },
